comments.body:
@participant3 my use case involve links to other Streamlit pages with specific parameters. I show overview information about several instances of a thing in the form of a table and then provide a link for a drill-down analysis of each one, like so:

![image](https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/assets/15786333/6dc88585-06f8-45e6-930c-4defd48a60eb)

Ideally for me, to minimize space, the text in "kpi_id" would be clickable directing to the  URLs in "inspect". I guess this would be solution 3 from @reporter original proposition. But the "inspect" column with a fixed text (e.g. "Inspect") directing to the URL would be equally fine, i.e. solution 2.
